        "collapsible_row_7P7Uia": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Sizing",
            "anchor_id": "",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p><br/>Sizing assistance is available for in-stock and custom pieces. </p><p>For rings, a complimentary ring sizer can be mailed to you, or you can follow our sizing PDF.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_3tNhhR": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "CARE",
            "anchor_id": "",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p><br/>Each Lloyd Steven piece is made to be worn everyday and last a lifetime. </p><p>Fine jewellery is durable, but not static. With regular wear, surfaces will soften and metals will develop a natural patina. These changes are considered part of the life of the piece.</p><p><strong><br/><br/>GENERAL CARE<br/></strong>When not in use, store jewellery in a dry, dark place — ideally in its original box or a dedicated jewellery case.</p><p>Avoid direct contact with perfumes, lotions, sunscreens, and household cleaning products. Jewellery is best put on after dressing and removed before cleaning, bathing, or swimming.<br/></p><p><strong><br/><br/>STERLING SILVER<br/></strong>Sterling silver should be stored in a cool, dry environment. <br/><br/>Prolonged exposure to moisture or chlorinated water may cause oxidation and a tarnished appearance. Remove silver jewellery prior to swimming, bathing or sport.</p><p><strong><br/><br/>CLEANING<br/></strong>For regular care, gently polish jewellery with a soft microfiber cloth.</p><p>To clean dirt from engraved areas, use warm water, mild soap, and a soft-bristled toothbrush. Avoid chemical jewellery cleaners and ultrasonic cleaning devices, particularly on plated or ceramic-finished pieces.</p><p><strong><br/><br/>MATERIALS + SOURCING<br/></strong>Materials are selected with care and intention. Stones are sourced individually, with attention to quality, character, and suitability for each design. Certification is provided where applicable.</p><p><strong> <br/><br/>RING SIZING<br/></strong>Accurate sizing is essential. We recommend having your finger measured by a professional jeweller prior to confirming size. Finger size can vary with temperature and time of day.</p><p>Sizing assistance is available by appointment, or we can provide a complimentary ring sizer.</p><p>If you have questions regarding care, sizing, or wear, please contact the studio.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
